course: dictionary
lesson: 8791
title: Shape: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word shape can mean different things, so read the words around it to find the right meaning. Ask yourself what the sentence is about: a form, a figure in maths, or someone's fitness.
explain: «A triangle frame keeps its shape when pushed, but a square frame can be pushed out of shape.» Here shape means the form or outline of something. Out of shape means its form has changed, so the square frame no longer looks the way it did.
explain: Shape can also be a verb. To shape something is to make it into a certain form, like shaping clay. «In good shape» is different again: it means fit and healthy. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A shape is the outline or form of something.
fact: Square and triangle are flat 2-D shapes; cube and sphere are solid 3-D shapes.
fact: To shape something is to make it into a certain form, like shaping clay.
fact: «In good shape» means fit and healthy or in good condition.
fact: «Take shape» means to start to look finished.
exercise: «A triangle frame keeps its shape when pushed, but a square frame can be pushed out of shape.» What does shape mean in «out of shape»? | A colour it has | *Its form or outline, so it is no longer the same | The sound it makes
exercise: Which one is a 3-D shape? | *Cube | Triangle | Square | Circle
exercise: Ella says, «Grandad is in good shape for his age.» What does in good shape mean? | Lost in a maze | *Fit and healthy | Painted in bright colours | Made of clay
test: «In a liquid like juice the particles stay close but slide past each other, so the juice takes the shape of a tall glass or a wide bowl.» What does takes the shape mean here? | *Fits the form of the container it is in | Changes its colour | Is made of clay | Goes cold
test: Shaping clay means | To weigh it | To break it | To paint it | *To make it into a certain form
exam: «The pysanka museum in Kolomyia is shaped like a giant egg.» What does shaped mean here? | Coloured with bright dyes | *Made into the form of | Lost its outline | Counted in groups
